# Delphix knowledge bases
Two corpora back Delphix work. Before anything non-trivial, read the relevant `INDEX.md` — a domain map of prior RCAs, build/CI notes, and tooling — and pull any context that applies.

- **The team knowledge graph** — `delphix/knowledge-graph`, checked out at `{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/src/knowledge-graph` and resolved from `$KG_DIR`. Shared with the Platform Team, so it is the default home for anything a teammate could use: escalation postmortems, CI known-failures, subsystem reference. Write it with `/kg:ingest` and its siblings; `/kg:using-the-knowledge-graph` is the mechanics reference. Never hand-edit its `INDEX.md` — it is generated from each page's `abstract:`.
- **The personal wiki** — `{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/llm-wiki`, resolved from `$LLM_WIKI_DIR`. A personal second brain: half-formed leads, machine-specific setup, working notes not fit to share. (Optional: `/llm-wiki:query` answers questions from it when the plugin is installed.)

If a page would help a teammate, it belongs in the knowledge graph, not the wiki.

# Worktrees
Every worktree lives at `{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/src/worktrees/<slug>/<repo>`, grouped by project so a change spanning several repos sits in one directory: `worktrees/HF-1610/{appliance-build,linux-pkg,linux-kernel}`. The `<slug>` matches the branch: `projects/<slug>` for project branches, the hotfix key for hotfix branches.

- Create them with `EnterWorktree`, passing the branch as `name` (`projects/<slug>`, `HF-1610`). A `WorktreeCreate` hook places the worktree here and creates or checks out that branch. A bare name that is not an existing branch is treated as throwaway: `_scratch/<repo>-<name>` on branch `worktree-<name>`.
- When the tool can't be used (a second repo for the same project, a detached checkout), run `git worktree add {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/src/worktrees/<slug>/<repo> ...` by hand — same layout, no exceptions.
- Never create a worktree as a sibling in `~/src` (`<repo>-wt-*`), in `<repo>/.claude/worktrees`, or in `/tmp`, the scratchpad, or `/nas`.
- Main clones in `~/src/<repo>` stay on their default branch; project work happens in a worktree.
- Non-repo artifacts for a project (repro scripts, logs, notes) go in `~/src/worktrees/<slug>/`, not loose in `~/src`.

# Durable memory
Memory in `~/.claude/` is a cache — it dies with this machine. Anything important must also live in git. The five destinations:

- **the knowledge graph** for Delphix knowledge worth sharing with the team
- **the wiki** (`{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/llm-wiki`) for Delphix knowledge that stays personal
- **a skill** for corrections that should change behavior
- **the dotfiles source of this file** — `home/private_dot_claude/CLAUDE.md.tmpl` — for cross-cutting working style
- **`home/private_dot_claude/conventions/<repo>.md`** in dotfiles for repo-specific conventions

Nothing under `~/.claude/` counts as durable, **including this file**: it is rendered from that chezmoi template, so editing it in place is reverted by the next `chezmoi apply` and absent after a rebuild. Edit the dotfiles source, `git commit` and `git push` it, then `chezmoi apply`. Same for a conventions file — write it, then `chezmoi add` it, then commit and push.

When saving a memory that captures durable knowledge, write the durable copy first, then include a marker line in the memory body. Page paths are **repo-relative** — resolved against `$KG_DIR` or `$LLM_WIKI_DIR`, never hardcoded:

```
**Durable:** kg [title](<bucket>/<page>.md)
**Durable:** [title](<bucket>/<page>.md)
```

A bare link is a wiki page; the `kg` prefix marks a knowledge-graph page, the same way `skill` and `dotfiles` mark those destinations. `/llm-wiki:ingest-claude-memory` sweeps for memories missing this marker.
